# REQUIRES: python-api
# The Lennard-Jones table tunable by pairs of types (D[python-tunable-pairs],
# #160): an update during a run that breaks the combining rule equals, to the
# bit, a compile with the new values; on the CPU in double precision the change
# of the energy against a NumPy sum over the table, pair and per-type tunables
# together, refusals, and the correction for the dispersion against its formula.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide pairs CPU Double | FileCheck %s --check-prefixes=CHECK,NUMPY
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_tunable.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide pairs CPU Mixed | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: CPU {{Double|Mixed}}: pairs: an update at step 6 off the combining rule and 10 steps equal a compile with the new values from that state to the bit
# NUMPY: pairs: the change of the energy at fixed positions
# NUMPY: pairs with per-type tunables: the change of the energy
# NUMPY: pairs: refusals and the warning of a pair that keeps a value of its own
# NUMPY: pairs: the correction for the dispersion at the new pair values
# CHECK: pairs passed
